' Artifact: CapsuleAI Implementation View
' Version: 0.1; Status: Baseline Draft; Date: 2026-10-10
' Source: ADD v0.1 (authoring input navigation v0.1.1); Selected Architecture Decisions v0.1.2,
' ADA-001-018 Selected; approved Logical View v0.1, re-read immediately before drawing.
' Later navigation-only patches leave these design/selection inputs unchanged.
' Logical acceptance: explicit human statement in the Implementation View task, 2026-10-10.
' Navigation update only, 2026-10-11: all three preceding views human-accepted; Data v0.1 exists.
' Accepted source/module structure unchanged; Data View review precedes ADRs.
' Scope: source modules/components, Clean roles, dependency direction, ports/adapters/contracts.
' Not in scope: deployment nodes, physical DB schema, endpoint details or full class design.
' Process: Initial files/CapsuleAI_Scrum_Development_Workflow.md Sections 22/39-43/46.
' Requirements: BRD v0.3, PRD v0.2, SRS v0.3, Business Rules v0.1.2; all 23 UCs/12 ADs.
' Drivers: existing seven AD-01-07 and nine ASRs; ADD Sections 7-10/12-13; no new obligation.
'
' Logical -> proposed Java package relative to an unresolved application root:
' Identity -> identity; UC-001-004, FR-AUTH, BRULE-AUTH, ADA-008/009.
' Personal Context -> personalcontext; UC-005/006, FR-PROF/WEATHER, BRULE-PROF.
' Wardrobe -> wardrobe; UC-007-010, FR-AI/GAR/WAR, BRULE-GAR, ADA-004/005/007.
' Outfit Advice and Use -> outfitadviceanduse; UC-011-018, BRULE-OUT/PERS/WEAR/HIST.
' Outfit Evaluation Semantics -> outfitadviceanduse.api policy contract + private domain realization.
' Wardrobe Intelligence -> wardrobeintelligence; UC-019-023, BRULE-COV/GAP/MULT/SHOP.
' Product Measurement -> productmeasurement; supporting only, FR-MET-001-007/DATA-RET-003.
' Packages represent source boundaries, not separate build artifacts, JPMS modules or services.
' The diagram proposes role-level names, not a finalized catalogue of Java interfaces/classes.
'
' Each module: api is its narrow framework-free public collaboration surface.
' application coordinates use cases, implements API and depends on private domain + needed ports.
' application.ports describes required persistence/integration/neighbor outcomes, not generic CRUD.
' adapter.in translates mobile/local-event input; adapter.out implements needed ports.
' Neighbor adapters import only supplier api, translate only genuine differences in meaning.
' Each module's configuration wires its own private implementations; root bootstrap delegates
' assembly to those configurations. Spring transaction/client/security integration stays outer,
' with no domain policy or bootstrap imports of another owner's private implementation.
' Grouped adapters represent several focused implementations, not one universal adapter class.
' Public contract models are owner-controlled language; no private aggregate/entity exposure.
'
' Immediate coordination: current authority, garment exclusion/readiness, profile withdrawal,
' new Wear ownership validation, survivor effects and same-basis assessments use public owners.
' Application owns invariant participants and durable logical-action outcome; outer transaction
' wiring may coordinate local ACID through public operations, never another owner's repository.
' New Wear: Outfit Advice and Use coordinates Wardrobe current ownership/readiness participation.
' Garment removal does not call back into Outfit Advice and Use; current owner queries exclude
' removed inputs, and minimal historical snapshots preserve necessary past meaning independently.
' Wardrobe detail composition belongs to inbound use-case coordination: public Wardrobe and
' reported-use APIs, no Wardrobe domain/application dependency on Outfit private internals.
' Identity owns persisted session/reset authority; usable JWT is necessary but insufficient.
' Protected callers consume usable authority and owners enforce affected-information ownership.
' Repeated security/measurement arrows omitted; omission grants no authorization bypass.
'
' Evaluation policy receives caller-supplied published inputs including Wardrobe readiness meaning.
' It does not fetch a Daily ranked subset or current owner state; Intelligence owns full-set
' orchestration and uses the same policy without duplicating identity/hard-validity rules.
' Outfit identity uses garment-identity sets; owned/historical/hypothetical meaning stays distinct.
' Same-basis current/expanded completeness governs Exact/Evaluated Zero and candidate previews;
' Incomplete/Unavailable/Outdated remain honest outcomes. No assessment TTL or projection store.
' Candidates, previews and chosen navigation create neither garment ownership nor Wear.
'
' Independent measurement: one representative local Domain/Application Event relationship.
' This is a notification dependency, not a requirement to import private listener implementations.
' The supporting public intake contract defines permitted outcome meaning; payload/dispatch open.
' Failure cannot block/reverse accepted core action or claim successful evidence recording.
' No automatic async/durability/replay claim; required physical lifecycle work is owner-accountable,
' durable/resumable and reached through owner application/ports, not optional measurement.
' Product Measurement persistence covers its limited-purpose evidence/lifecycle, not core history.
' Intelligence persistence covers only justified owned source/action/work state; derived results
' remain request-time and do not require a permanent result store or replicated owner data.
'
' Boundary enforcement: allow imports only to other modules' api; deny private domain/application/
' ports/adapter/repository/entity imports. Inside modules, domain imports no Spring/persistence/
' HTTP/JSON/provider models; application uses domain + its own ports/public contract language.
' Wiring is outer and one-way. Reviews and later dependency checks enforce these rules;
' Java public visibility/component scanning alone is not enforcement. Exact tooling unselected.
' Audit: no business-context cycle; the use-case composition component is an inbound consumer,
' not a reverse domain collaboration. Realization arrows implement ports, not runtime call order.
' Extraction: each owner retains public API, policy and owned persistence/provider boundaries.
' Remote authority/freshness calls, new-Wear owner participation and coherent assessed bases
' would require explicit distributed consistency/failure redesign; no extraction driver found.
' Pure published evaluation avoids Intelligence -> Daily -> owner call chains.
'
' Review uncertainty: exact package root/names/build split, persistence framework, Spring/JDK,
' enforcement tooling, event dispatch/payload/phase, transaction/locking/action keys/retention,
' provider clients/protocols/timeouts, work scheduling and Python internal source organization.
' No JPA/Hibernate, external provider/version, build tool or deployment placement selected here.
' Current-doc checks (Context7, 2026-10-10) explain capabilities, not project version selection:
' https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/reference/using/structuring-your-code.html
' https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/reference/core/beans/context-introduction.html
' https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/reference/data-access/transaction/event.html
' https://plantuml.com/component-diagram and https://plantuml.com/command-line
' Default Spring listeners are synchronous; transaction phase alone does not provide durable replay.

