legend bottom
  |= Notation |= Source-architecture meaning |
  | Soft module color | Approved logical owner -> proposed Java package; one core application. |
  | Stronger tint; <<public>> / <<public policy>> | Owner-controlled, framework-free published contract language. |
  | Pale tint; <<private core>> / <<private ports>> | Application -> domain / needed ports; private owner policy. |
  | Near-white; <<private adapter>> | Inbound translation or outbound port implementation; framework/provider edge. |
  | Solid arrow | Consumer depends on named public contract, own policy/port, or external resource. |
  | Dotted triangle | Private implementation realizes contract/port; not runtime call direction. |
  | Pink dotted event | Independent local notification; not automatically async, durable or an Integration Event. |
  Consumers import supplier api only; module configuration wires its private implementations.
  Grouped port/adapter roles do not mandate one interface/class or an interface for every class.
  All protected owners use current Identity authority and enforce affected-information ownership.
  Application coordinates public owners / durable action outcomes; local ACID is allowed.
  Immediate withdrawal, Wear survivor effects and assessment basis remain coherent at acceptance.
  External media/email effects and owner-required resumable lifecycle work are explicit.
  Evaluation policy stays inside Outfit Advice and Use; caller inputs, no Daily subset dependency.
  Measurement failure cannot block/reverse core acceptance or fabricate recorded evidence.
  No dedicated cache/broker, shared entities, internal network calls or unrestricted DB access.
  Exact packages, libraries, versions, enforcement, event/transaction mechanics remain open.
  Next: Data View review -> ADRs.
endlegend
@enduml
